@startuml storage-layout
title Legacy readable-token view: M-CB4: persistent storage / runtime socket - broker v0, design only

component "swarma-credential-broker daemon\nunprivileged service UID\nLaunchDaemon UserName / systemd User" as Broker
component "Operator command\nswarma-operator; no harness or shell" as Operator
component "Read-only client\nswarma-observer; no harness" as Observer
component "Phone app\noperator device key: secure element\nprivate key never leaves; biometric presence" as Phone
actor "Person" as Person
folder "Protected swarma-operator account storage\nnever an agent/session account; locator unpublished" as OperatorHome {
  artifact "Broker v0 Ed25519 software-root private key\nmode 0600; existing broker envelope signatures" as Root
  artifact "Operator records / authority\nteam/1, standing retirement, maintenance,\nexplicit home retention, standing re-grants" as OperatorRecords
  artifact "Pinned phone public key / operator command policy\nprotected from agent accounts; layout unpublished" as PhonePin
}
component "swarma-dispatcher\nown service OS account" as Dispatcher
component "curator-run\nactive agent UID + generation" as Executor
component "swarma-user-manager\nroot; ledger publisher" as Helper
component "Existing service manager\nrestore start check; qualified writer containment" as Manager
component "Approved Codex executable\nbroker UID; pinned digest; slice 1" as Codex

folder "Broker service home: /opt/swarma/services/swarma-credential-broker\nbroker UID owns all files; directories 0700 (§15.1-§15.2)" as Home {
  artifact "Configuration\nprincipal pins, approved endpoints/executables, root public keys" as Config
  artifact "Account records\nmetadata only; vendor ID, state, expiry (possibly unknown)" as Accounts
  artifact "Secret store\n0600 files in 0700 directory\nClaude setup-token / API or business tokens" as Secrets
  folder "Fresh broker-owned Codex home (slice 1)" as CodexHome {
    artifact "Vendor login\naccess + refresh material, file credential storage" as Login
  }
  artifact "Stable lock beside Codex home\nread / refresh / reload serialisation" as Lock
  artifact "Grant envelopes\nsigned public authorisation metadata" as Grants
  artifact "Revocation state {seq, records}\nauthoritative local state" as Revocations
  artifact "Binding records and receiver journal/tombstones\nUID + generation; admission-class evidence;\nchains; bind/unbind effect evidence" as Bindings
  artifact "Durable refresh attempt evidence\nintent before launch; prior outcome / process identity" as Attempts
  artifact "Durable time watermark / elapsed evidence\ntrusted advances, expiry/reset history; layout unpublished" as Time
  artifact "R-ALLSTOP freeze / recovery journal\nlogical record; layout and intake unpublished" as Freeze
  artifact "Lease records\nowner tuple + launch/policy metadata; NEVER payload" as Leases
  artifact "Append-only audit log\ntyped principal/account/launch/outcome metadata\nno material, raw frames, secret errors or token hashes" as Audit
}

folder "Runtime socket directory: /opt/swarma/run/credential-broker/\nbroker UID; 0755; ancestors root-owned, not writable by others" as Runtime {
  artifact "Unix-domain socket\n0666; authorisation by kernel peer principal\nsocket basename unspecified in spec §15.2" as Socket
}
artifact "Outside restored failure domain\noperator restore mark; surviving history/checkpoint evidence\nand durable reconciliation/reopen decision\ntime restore/expiry-reset evidence; location/format unpublished (§18.8, §18.12)" as Restore
artifact "Helper ledger: /opt/swarma/lib/user-manager/ledger.json\nroot-owned 0644, root-owned directory; no secrets\nconfigured installation root changes this locator (§4.2)" as Ledger

Person --> Phone : exact act shown; biometric confirmation
Phone --> Operator : SSH over tailnet; key only; forced command; signed canonical act
Person --> Operator : terminal sudo: password, timestamp_timeout=0, no NOPASSWD
Operator --> PhonePin : verify signature bound to this exact act
Operator --> Root : sign existing broker envelope after operator admission
Operator --> OperatorRecords : admitted operator acts
Operator --> Socket : admitted owner/operator methods
Observer --> Socket : status / account.list / grant.list / binding.list; no confirmation
Dispatcher --> Socket : bind with admission class (encoding unpublished) / unbind; effect.observe; revocation.check
Executor --> Socket : fresh agent-side lease connection
Socket --> Broker : broker/1; no network listener
Broker --> Config : read configuration
Broker --> Accounts : account metadata
Broker --> Secrets : put / get / delete / describe (§5.3)
Broker --> Grants : signed grants
Broker --> Revocations : publish under shared state lock (§6.4)
Broker --> Bindings : bind / unbind records
Broker --> Freeze : durable freeze before acknowledgement; explicit recovery evidence
Broker --> Leases : persist without payload (§8.3)
Broker --> Audit : append (§12.3)
Broker --> Lock : internal per-account auth owner locks
Broker --> Attempts : persist intent before launch; resolve prior attempt
Broker --> Time : persist before authority release; boot-inclusive elapsed accounting
Broker --> Manager : contained writer lifecycle; stop / confirm absence
Manager --> Codex : qualified containment / kill-and-confirm
Manager --> Restore : start check before opening authorization
Operator --> Restore : fence before snapshot restore; reconcile/reopen last
Broker --> Codex : approved enrol / refresh after lifecycle and outcome gate
Codex --> Login : vendor writes broker-owned login
Helper --> Ledger : atomic replacement + flush / rename / directory flush
Broker --> Ledger : direct read at bind / lease / renew; never home fallback

note bottom of Home
  State files replaced atomically within their own directory (§12.4).
  Revocations: temp write, flush, rename, directory flush, update memory,
  then acknowledgement under lock shared with material release (§6.4).
  Audit append-only is separate from state-file replacement (§12.3).
  Except the helper ledger, basenames and split of files/directories
  unspecified in spec §5.3 / §12.4 / §15.2; boxes are logical records.
  Modes for non-secret state files unspecified in spec §12.4;
  no claimed 0600 blanket beyond the specified secret backend.
  [[../spec/broker.md#53-secret-store Spec §5.3]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#124-files Spec §12.4]]
end note
note right of Broker
  Startup refuses if store/config or any parent directory is writable
  by another user (§12.4). Kernel peer identity unavailable: refuse (§4.1).
  Revocation read/parse failure: all leases/renewals refuse until
  operator repairs; never restart from empty state (§6.4).
  Ledger mismatch/read failure: principal_ledger_mismatch (§4.2).
  Fenced restore blocks authorization and auto-start (§15.4);
  revocation.check unavailable, even with a readable old snapshot.
  Complete surviving history or explicit old-root replacement/reissue
  is required before durable reopen/readiness, then auto-start last.
  Concrete start integration and audit write-failure response:
  unpublished (§18.8 / §12.3).
end note
note bottom of Runtime
  Socket lives outside the data tree; clients verify broker peer UID
  before sending. Socket mode is access, not authority (§4.1).
  Lease payload travels only to executor/harness; no launch credential file.
  [[../spec/broker.md#152-paths Spec §15.2]]
end note
note right of CodexHome
  Only auth owner uses this home; refresh token never leaves broker (§9).
  No imported home/login or exported keyring item (§9.2).
  At most one live writer across daemon replacement (§9.4).
  Prior writer must be contained, killed and confirmed absent;
  recover attempt and durable home before deciding retry safety.
  Ambiguous external rotation: no blind retry even after child absence;
  stay unavailable or re-enrol after absence. Safe transient failures
  alone permit backoff; platform mechanisms unpublished (§18.10).
  Launch app-server runs under agent UID with ephemeral credentials,
  no launch auth.json; account storage above is a separate boundary (§9.3).
end note
note bottom of Secrets
  Muse native login store is separate from this v0 broker file backend (§10.2).
  PROPOSED (b): one minting owner retains OAuth tokens and leases only
  the minted provider API key via META_API_KEY / exec --api-key-stdin.
  Native macOS store: Keychain-first, file fallback; file writes replace
  the inode, so children never share a linked store. No new location assigned.
  Fallback (c): key not subscription-billed or revoked by re-mint.
  Qualification remains open (§18.5); explicit API-key lane stays separate.
end note
note left of Home
  Uninstall: close admission/auto-start; stop service and kill-confirm
  vendor writers; unknown cleanup defers removal. End leases/bindings,
  retain effect/removal evidence; keep store unless
  operator requests destruction (§15.3). Removal/secure-erasure
  algorithm, audit retention and garbage collection unspecified
  in spec §15.3 / §12.3. Copied tokens need expiry/vendor revoke (§12.1).
  [[../spec/broker.md#153-removal Spec §15.3]]
end note
note top of Operator
  Software-root private key: swarma-operator custody (§4.3), no harness.
  Phone device key is separate; broker signature algorithm unchanged.
  Widening requires authentication + exact content confirmation;
  refused in agent sessions; narrowing requires authentication only.
  Phone revocation: one biometric confirmation, no extra content prompt.
  Binary/wire format, domain/canonical bytes and phone-key lifecycle
  unpublished (§18.15); terminal re-enrolment is the recovery proposal.
  Keychain / Secret Service later, not v0 (§5.3).
  Keeper adapter later; Codex slice 1 still pending qualification (§18.4).
  SH1/SH2 activation unspecified in spec §3.1.
end note
note bottom of Time
  R-TIME: expiry checked at max(now, watermark), not_before at min(now, watermark).
  Untrusted time cannot advance watermark or release material.
  Expiry removal needs monotonic lifetime; missing evidence delays deletion.
  Reset is explicit operator act; genuinely expired rights stay expired (§15.1).
end note
note bottom of Broker
  R-SVC-EGRESS v1: only network destination is dedicated proxy listener;
  explicit vendor-child proxy config, login/refresh and resolver qualification.
  User manager §8 owns start/scheduled service-row re-verification.
  R-FATE user manager §7 owns fate table and previous-writer fence.
  R-LOCK state lock released for platform calls; per-record marker
  and late-result fences; account writer ownership remains (§13.1).
  R-GEN companion restore procedures reconcile ledger/effects (§15.4).
end note
note bottom of Bindings
  R-REBIND same UID/generation: old-binding tombstone and ended leases,
  then fresh binding ID; replay cannot reactivate or target replacement.
  R-OUTCOME bind/unbind tables retain the six R-OBS states (§13.2).
end note
note bottom of Freeze
  R-ALLSTOP freezes all leases/renewals and final post-refresh delivery;
  every service start checks freeze/recovery evidence (§15.5).
  Partial/unknown/unreadable results keep admission closed; no automatic restart.
  Delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime. No new file basename or state enum.
  R-UNTRUSTED admission evidence retained for UID/generation; no binding/lease
  for untrusted or unavailable class. Encodings/codes unpublished (§18.16-§18.17).
end note
@enduml

@startuml storage-layout-secret-free
!theme plain
title Proposed secret-free view: storage-layout — inactive
component "Agent account\nplaceholder only" as A
component "Broker lifecycle service" as B
component "Separate gateway / action service" as G
database "Protected broker custody\ncredentials + refresh owner\nservice/caller bindings and lease metadata\naccount hold + issued-version inventory\nrevocation/restore/stop evidence" as S
database "Protected spending-service evidence\ncurrent authority / policy generation\nqueues, stream closure and effect outcomes\nbudgets survive restart" as U
B --> S : durable state; lease metadata has no payload
B --> G : admitted service lease material
G --> U : retain fences and UNKNOWN outcomes
A --> G : own current listener mapping only
note bottom of S
  All issued still-vendor-valid versions remain matchable,
  even after refresh/release; expiry or confirmed invalidation ends validity.
  Existing protected store/time/restore primitives unchanged.
  No new filenames, record enums or transaction formats assigned.
end note
note bottom of A
  No vendor credential/home/keyring/private service pipe access.
  Outside-gateway matcher custody OPEN; no raw inventory to bridge/LLM.
end note

legend bottom
  Separate proposed secret-free mode, document revision 1: INACTIVE / UNQUALIFIED.
  Semantic responsibilities only; no new v0 methods, fields, codes or record formats.
  [[../spec/secret-free-mode.md Owning proposed contract and qualification gates]]
endlegend
@enduml
